###  https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#belongsToElectrode
battgpt:belongsToElectrode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain emmo:EMMO_df96cbb6_b5ee_4222_8eab_b3675df24bea ;
                           rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        owl:unionOf ( battgpt:NegativeElectrodeRole
                                                      battgpt:PositiveElectrodeRole
                                                    )
                                      ] ;
                           rdfs:comment "Relates a chemical substance (EMMO ChemicalSubstance, not EMMO's separate Material class) to the specific electrode role (positive or negative) it plays. Range tightened (v0.3.0) to the union of the two electrode-role classes so it can no longer point at ElectrolyteRoleIndividual/SeparatorRoleIndividual, which the property's name never intended. The owl:inverseOf link to usesMaterial was REMOVED in v0.3.2: with the inverse in place, this property's narrowed range propagated onto usesMaterial's subjects, so any usesMaterial assertion made from an ElectrolyteRole or SeparatorRole individual entailed that individual was a Positive- or NegativeElectrodeRole, which contradicts the v0.3.1 role disjointness axiom and made such graphs inconsistent. usesMaterial is therefore now an independent property, genuinely general over all four BatteryRole subclasses as always intended, while belongsToElectrode keeps its electrode-only range."@en ;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#> ;
                           rdfs:label "belongsToElectrode"@en ;
                           skos:prefLabel "belongsToElectrode"@en .


