###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_df96cbb6_b5ee_4222_8eab_b3675df24bea (EMMO ChemicalSubstance — extended here, not locally defined; see usesMaterial's comment for why this class rather than EMMO's separate Material class is used throughout)
emmo:EMMO_df96cbb6_b5ee_4222_8eab_b3675df24bea
        rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty emmo:EMMO_e1097637_70d2_4895_973f_2396f04fa204 ;
                           owl:someValuesFrom emmo:EMMO_b7bcff25_ffc3_474e_9ab5_01b1664bd4ba
                         ] ;
        rdfs:comment "BattGPT extension axiom on the imported ChemicalSubstance class: requires at least one emmo:hasProperty value of type emmo:Property. Deliberately weak — satisfied by any single one of hasBandGap, hasBulkModulus, hasEnergyAboveHull, hasFormationEnergy, or hasShearModulus (all subPropertyOf hasProperty, domain ChemicalSubstance, range a Property subclass) being populated, not a requirement that all five be present. Does not cover hasStructure, which is subPropertyOf hasPart rather than hasProperty and is intentionally left unconstrained on this class (see CrystalStructure's comment) since not every chemical substance in this KG's scope is expected to have a resolved crystal structure. This axiom reaches every ChemicalSubstance individual in any dataset ever loaded alongside this ontology, not only BattGPT's own materials — kept deliberately weak for that reason rather than requiring each specific quantity individually, since none of the five is always computed or even physically meaningful for every substance (e.g. elastic moduli for a liquid electrolyte)."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_68ed592a_7924_45d0_a108_94d6275d57f0 (EMMO/BattINFO BatteryCell — extended here, not locally defined)
battery:battery_68ed592a_7924_45d0_a108_94d6275d57f0
        rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty emmo:EMMO_8e52c42b_e879_4473_9fa1_4b23428b392b ;
                           owl:someValuesFrom battgpt:BatteryRole
                         ] ;
        rdfs:comment "BattGPT extension axiom on the imported BatteryCell class: requires at least one emmo:hasRole value of type battgpt:BatteryRole. Reuses EMMO's own Role/Whole/hasRole mechanism (hasRole domain=Whole, range=Role; BatteryRole is already subClassOf Role) rather than inventing a new property — no new property was created for this. BatteryCell's own EMMO definition already describes it as 'an assembly of electrodes, electrolyte, container, terminals and usually separators', i.e. a Whole whose defining parts include role-players; this axiom formalizes that. Because hasRole's domain is emmo:Whole, this restriction entails BatteryCell is a Whole via domain propagation, so no separate subClassOf Whole assertion is needed. Establishes the path BatteryCell -hasRole-> BatteryRole -usesMaterial-> ChemicalSubstance, which was previously unconnected. Verified in a disposable test copy under both ROBOT+ELK and ROBOT+HermiT (full merged closure): introduces zero new unsatisfiable classes; the ontology still shows only the same two pre-existing, EMMO-internal unsatisfiable classes (CentiMetreSecondDegreeCelsius, MagneticMoment) that exist with or without this axiom."@en .


