###  https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#CrystalStructure
battgpt:CrystalStructure rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty battgpt:hasCrystalSystem ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom battgpt:CrystalSystem
                                         ] ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty battgpt:hasSpaceGroup ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom battgpt:SpaceGroup
                                         ] ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty battgpt:hasUnitCell ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom battgpt:UnitCell
                                         ] ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty battgpt:hasStructureFamily ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom battgpt:StructureFamily
                                         ] ;
                         rdfs:comment "The periodic crystalline arrangement of a chemical substance — its unit cell, symmetry, and atomic sites — construed as a structural aspect of the substance itself rather than as a document or description about it. This reading is what the formal axioms assert (v0.3.2 wording clarification, replacing the earlier phrase 'structural representation' which read as a semiotic artefact): hasStructure is a subproperty of emmo:hasPart, itself a subproperty of emmo:overlaps, so a chemical substance and its CrystalStructure are entailed to share parts — coherent for a physical arrangement, incoherent for a description of one. The serialised description of this structure is carried separately as a literal by hasCif. Explicitly anchored under owl:Thing (v0.3.0) for consistency with its sibling local classes (Site, UnitCell, Species, CrystalBond); no single class in EMMO core, EMMO domain-battery, EMMO domain-electrochemistry, or EMMO domain-chemical-substance cleanly captures 'the crystallographic structure of a substance', and EMMO's own domain-crystallography ontology remains an explicitly work-in-progress v0.1.0 draft not imported here, so this is left as a standalone local root rather than force-fit under an unstable upstream branch. Requires at least one hasUnitCell, hasSpaceGroup, and hasStructureFamily value (v0.3.1), and one hasCrystalSystem value, matching what RDFValidator already enforced at the data level. The hasStructureFamily requirement means every populated CrystalStructure must be classified into one of the 9 curated structure-family leaves (StructureFamily's subclasses) — a genuinely novel prototype not fitting any of them would need a new leaf class added before it could be populated."@en ;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#> ;
                         rdfs:label "CrystalStructure"@en ;
                         rdfs:seeAlso <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Supercell_(crystal)> ;
                         skos:prefLabel "CrystalStructure"@en .


